WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions for the voiceover only. The film's own on-screen lines are burned in and
are deliberately not repeated here. Cue boundaries come from the speech onsets in
the mixed audio, not from the scene table in VO-SCRIPT.md, so they track the read
rather than the storyboard.

1
00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:09.210
Claude Code is a text editor.
runcastle is the IDE around it.

2
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.170
Every feature you build gets its own session.

3
00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.550
Name it, size it, go.

4
00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:19.150
A real Claude Code session opens with your brief, your repo

5
00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:21.570
and the phase rules already injected —

6
00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.410
and it grills you until the idea is actually concrete.

7
00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.680
The decisions get written down and committed.

8
00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.960
To your repo, under docs/features.

9
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.370
It outlives the tool.

10
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.420
Then the spec is split: atomic tickets, in dependency order.

11
00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:40.180
One click.

12
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:44.010
That's the first of two times runcastle stops for you.

13
00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:51.530
Sandboxed agents pick up every unblocked ticket at once,

14
00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:53.500
in containers, on your machine.

15
00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:57.190
Blocked ones wait for their dependency and then go.

16
00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.850
Commits land on one branch.

17
00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.700
You can watch it — every edit, every test,

18
00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.140
every commit, streamed live.

19
00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:05.110
Or don't.

20
00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:07.450
Because this is one feature.

21
00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:08.660
Run four.

22
00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:11.820
Grill the next one while the last one builds —

23
00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:14.440
switching features is switching tabs.

24
00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:18.530
When it's done: drive the branch on its own port, then merge.

25
00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:19.500
That's click two.

26
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.900
Human in the loop at exactly the two ends.

27
00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.170
runcastle. Grill it, burn it, merge it.

28
00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:27.820
MIT, and it runs entirely on your machine.
